REQUEST_VERSION 1.0.0

ID REQUEST-0009

STATUS PENDING

DATE 2026-07-25

WHO President Cley Duarte

SCOPE PACE

TITLE

Per-chat memory that stores EVERYTHING shared in a conversation so an AI
always answers with full lucidity, never just the last thing said ("no
senile dementia").

RAW_TEXT

Even within an AI's own chat, it ages very early and gets senile dementia.
On every message it should go and consult PACE, and in PACE there must be a
structure created for each chat, so it never gets senile dementia. That
structure has to store everything shared in the chat and always be able to
answer with lucidity. Today, on long chats it is frustrating because it
seems the AI only remembers the last thing we talked about.

PROPOSED_SCOPE PACE

DESIGN_NOTE

Extends the Bootstrap/Handoff idea from "load context at session start" to
"re-ground on every turn". PACE keeps, per chat, a living context capsule
that stores the WHOLE conversation's substance — objective, every decision
taken, open threads, relevant history, latest state — not a recency window.
The AI reads it at the start of every turn and writes it back at the end,
so lucidity does not decay as the model's context window fills. PACE
provides the structure and protocol; the AI client wires the per-turn
read/write (part of the integration story). Candidate home: memory/ or a
new sessions/ area, governed by a future Session-Continuity protocol.

PROMOTED_TO

